[E0436] Error: `doubled` is used after `scale`, which it captures, was assigned
    ╭─[ err/439_function_variable_captured_and_changed/main.wip:16:17 ]
    │
 14 │     val doubled = (x: i64) => scale(x)
    │         ───┬───
    │            ╰───── `doubled` captures `scale`
 15 │     scale = (x: i64) => x * 3
    │     ──┬──
    │       ╰──── `scale` assigned here
 16 │     io::println("\(doubled(3))")
    │                    ───┬───
    │                       ╰───── used here
    │
    │ Help: call `doubled` before `scale` changes, or give it `scale` as an argument
    │
    │ Note: a closure kept in a `val` reads what it captures where it is, so that must not change while the closure is still used
────╯
[E0413] Error: `scale` is passed as `&var` together with another reference to it
    ╭─[ err/439_function_variable_captured_and_changed/main.wip:18:42 ]
    │
 18 │ ╭─▶     both((x) => io::println("\(scale(x))"), (x) => {
    │ │            ────────────────┬────────────────
    │ │                            ╰────────────────── a `&` reference
    ┆ ┆
 20 │ ├─▶     })
    │ │
    │ ╰──────────── a `&var` reference
    │
    │     Note: while a function runs, a `&var` argument must be the only reference to its place
────╯
